From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
Subject: [PATCH] SPARC64: return the whole physical address in phys.lo

The /memory "claim" and "SUNW,retain" methods and the /virtual-memory
"translate" method return a physical address as phys.lo phys.hi, with
phys.lo cut to its lower 32 bits. 64-bit clients read phys.lo alone:
NetBSD/sparc64's kernel and ofwboot (CELL2HDQ(hi, lo) is lo, and
HDQ2CELL_HI() is 0 when they pass an address in) and 64-bit Solaris
(p1275_cells2ull() on sparcv9). Above 4 GB they get the wrong address.

With 6 or 8 GB of RAM, ofwboot claims the pages for the NetBSD kernel
from the top of RAM, above 4 GB, maps its own allocations at the
truncated addresses (map 0x7fe7e000 for a claim that returned
0x17fe7e000), and the kernel's pages are not where NetBSD believes they
are. NetBSD 11.1 boots and runs until, with most of its memory in use,
its trap table is overwritten (apparently its own pages were handed out
as free), then stops:

  trap type 0x10: cpu 0, pc=1000d00 npc=1000d04 ...
  panic: illegal instruction

(while filling a tmpfs, at the same point with 6144 and 8192 MB).

Keep the whole address in phys.lo. phys.hi still carries the upper
32 bits, so a client that combines (phys.hi << 32) | phys.lo gets the
same address, and the methods that take an address in already decode
it that way.
---
 arch/sparc64/lib.c | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/sparc64/lib.c b/arch/sparc64/lib.c
index 1a5c9f1..822d999 100644
--- a/arch/sparc64/lib.c
+++ b/arch/sparc64/lib.c
@@ -138,7 +138,12 @@ mmu_translate(void)
     phys = ofmem_translate(virt, &mode);
 
     if (phys != -1UL) {
-		PUSH(phys & 0xffffffff);
+		/* 64-bit clients take the whole physical address from phys.lo
+		   and ignore phys.hi (NetBSD's CELL2HDQ(), Solaris'
+		   p1275_cells2ull() on sparcv9), so phys.lo must not be cut to
+		   32 bits. phys.hi keeps the upper bits for (hi << 32) | lo.
+		   The same for claim and retain */
+		PUSH(phys);
 		PUSH(phys >> 32);
 		PUSH(mode);
 		PUSH(-1);
@@ -375,7 +380,7 @@ mem_claim( void )
 
     phys = ofmem_claim_phys(phys, size, align);
 
-    PUSH(phys & 0xffffffffUL);
+    PUSH(phys);    /* phys.lo: the whole address, see mmu_translate() */
     PUSH(phys >> 32);
 }
 
@@ -414,7 +419,7 @@ mem_retain ( void )
 
     phys = ofmem_retain(phys, size, align);
 
-    PUSH(phys & 0xffffffffUL);
+    PUSH(phys);    /* phys.lo: the whole address, see mmu_translate() */
     PUSH(phys >> 32);
 }
 
